; Lower-priority threat policy zone.  Only QNAME, rpz-ip and rpz-ip6
; triggers and NXDOMAIN/NODATA/PASSTHRU actions are interpreted; anything
; else is reported as pending by the offline rehearsal.
;
; QNAME trigger owners are relative to $ORIGIN; the RPZ engine strips the
; zone origin before matching them against probe data names.
$ORIGIN threat.rpz.
$TTL 3600

@                       SOA ns1.example. hostmaster.example. (
                                2026111800 3600 900 86400 3600 )
@                       NS  ns1.example.

; --- QNAME triggers -------------------------------------------------------
evil.example            CNAME .                 ; legacy NXDOMAIN form
blocked.example         CNAME rpz-nxdomain.
quiet.example           CNAME rpz-nodata.
*.wild.example          CNAME rpz-nodata.
*.evil.example          CNAME rpz-nodata.
deep.more.evil.example  CNAME rpz-nxdomain.

; --- Response address triggers -------------------------------------------
; 192.0.2.0/32 (truncated reversed-octet owner)
32.2.0.192.rpz-ip       CNAME rpz-nxdomain.
; 8.8.8.0/24 and 8.8.0.0/16 exercise longest-prefix selection.
24.8.8.8.rpz-ip         CNAME .
16.8.8.rpz-ip           CNAME rpz-nodata.
; 2001:db8::/32 written as reversed nibbles.
32.8.b.d.0.1.0.0.2.rpz-ip6 CNAME rpz-nxdomain.

; --- Deliberately unsupported / pending content --------------------------
bad.ns.example.rpz-nsdname CNAME .              ; NSDNAME trigger
8.rpz-nsip                 CNAME .              ; NSIP trigger
*.16.10.rpz-ip             CNAME rpz-nxdomain.  ; wildcard address
mystery.example            CNAME rpz-tarpit.    ; unknown action
tarpit2.example            A 192.0.2.99         ; non-CNAME action RR
24.1.2.rpz-ip              CNAME rpz-drop.      ; legacy DROP action
99.1.2.rpz-ip              CNAME rpz-nxdomain.  ; prefix 99 > 32, malformed
